                <pb facs="0880" n="768" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg768"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 7370/33.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Mrs. Ove
                    Gude.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-07-02"><hi rendition="#italic">July 2,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Please accept the sincerest condolences in your sad bereavement. If the
                    Department of State can render any service pray be sure to command me. I offer
                    at the same time the deep personal sympathy of my wife and myself.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
